          "The framework then links those covered products to obligations that are addressed through the regulated system, including registration, reporting and relevant certificate transactions. Reported sales information, product categories and current rules determine what applies. The organisation should keep the underlying records that support the reported figures, reconcile unusual transactions and assign a reviewer who understands the source data. Do not treat an approximate weight of scrap removed from an office as the basis for a producer figure, and do not assume that donating equipment for reuse satisfies a statutory recycling requirement. Collection activity, regulatory transactions and reported obligations remain distinct pieces of evidence.",
